Ideas and lists borrowed from other projects
--------------------------------------------
No code was copied from any of them. No code under the GPL is used.

claude-moove   https://github.com/paulgegenyi/claude-moove   MIT License
    The list of what to copy from Claude's folders and what never to copy in
    manifests/*.json follows engine/README.md, checked on 2026-11-01. So does the
    list of rebuildable project folders, and the rule that build folders such as
    dist are left out only inside a git repository.
    Moving restored data to another computer (internal/restore/mapper.go) follows
    the rules of Set-PathMap and Convert-Text in engine/claude-moove.ps1, checked
    on 2026-11-03: the encoded name of a transcripts folder (every character that
    is not an ASCII letter or digit becomes a dash), paths matched without regard
    to case and only up to the end of a folder name, the three spellings of a
    path inside a file (as is, with doubled backslashes in JSON, with forward
    slashes), longest path first, and transcripts left unchanged while their
    folders are renamed. The restore refuses to put back Local Storage while
    Claude runs, as that project closes Claude for it. Copyright (c) 2026 Claude
    Moove contributors.

Claude Vault   https://github.com/Krimchanin/claude-vault    MIT License
    The search for Desktop data under %LOCALAPPDATA%\Packages\*\LocalCache\Roaming,
    %LOCALAPPDATA% and %APPDATA%, recognised by what the folder holds, follows
    detect_claude_root in src-tauri/src/lib.rs, checked on 2026-11-01. Unlike that
    function, BackUpClaude keeps every folder it finds, not only the first.
    The rule that putting restored files back only adds missing files and never
    replaces an existing one follows the README, checked on 2026-11-03.
    Copyright (c) 2026 Claude Vault contributors.
